  "reason": "The best result so far is config_047 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.586). All completed multimodal experiments used transformer aggregation, so we have no evidence about whether a simpler aggregation (avgpool) could match or exceed it, especially with the simpler linear PCA representation. Config_041 isolates the aggregation variable (transformer→avgpool) while keeping the top-performing RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and fusion (weighted) fixed. This is the highest-value exploitation step: if avgpool performs comparably, we confirm the design is robust; if it underperforms, we confirm transformer is essential and can focus remaining budget on other axes. With 4 experiments left, reducing uncertainty on this untested structural choice is more informative than the smaller fusion variation (weighted vs concat) where we already have directional evidence."
}

